TEXT 256 -272 Left 3 ;#87 Schmitt trigger RC oscillator
TEXT 256 -224 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NuXitMK3HSA
TEXT 256 -192 Left 2 ;A Schmitt inverter proxy charges and discharges the timing capacitor through feedback, making a square wave.
TEXT 920 -80 Left 2 !.ic V(RC)=0
TEXT 920 -24 Left 2 !.tran 0 5m 0 100n
TEXT 920 32 Left 2 !.meas tran T1 WHEN V(out)=2.5 RISE=3
TEXT 920 72 Left 2 !.meas tran T2 WHEN V(out)=2.5 RISE=4
TEXT 920 112 Left 2 !.meas tran PERIOD PARAM T2-T1
TEXT 920 152 Left 2 !.meas tran FREQ PARAM 1/(T2-T1)
TEXT 920 192 Left 2 !.meas tran VRC_UPPER MAX V(RC) FROM 1m TO 5m
TEXT 920 232 Left 2 !.meas tran VRC_LOWER MIN V(RC) FROM 1m TO 5m
TEXT 920 304 Left 2 ;Alan identifies R about 6.8k and C 47n at\n5:27-5:39. A1 is a generic Schmitt proxy,\nnot a 74AC14 model, so the thresholds are\nthe proxy's assumed ones and the frequency\nfollows from them.
